text:
Anya: proposal — introduce a lightweight Prefetch Broker to centralize prefetch decisions and issue short-lived prefetch leases. decouples decision logic from allocator, lets us do per-tenant rate limits and dedupe hints. thoughts?

Mike: sounds promising. how is this different from the existing prefetcher? especially around double-prefetching and interaction with residency state.

Sourav: key idea: broker hands out leases (id + ttl). workers perform prefetch and pin pages until lease expires or client releases. broker keeps simple state and budget counters. example hint payload: ```{
  "tenant": "acme",
  "hint": "prefix_hash:0xabc",
  "priority": "low"
}```

Katie: need to account for NUMA/topology. broker should accept preferred_node/allowed_nodes so prefetch workers can pick local pages. remote prefetch without pin-locality will kill perf.

Thomas: fairness concern — a noisy tenant could request many leases and saturate prefetch workers. broker must enforce per-tenant budgets + decay/backoff. also consider tenant priority classes.

Anya: agreed. plan: budget + soft quotas + backpressure signals returned to requesters; fallback becomes best-effort cache warmup instead of aggressive prefetch when budget exhausted.

Mike: telemetry wish list: prefetch_requests, leases_issued, prefetch_hits, prefetch_misses, avg_prefetch_latency, tenant_prefetch_budget_utilization. need these to tune defaults.

infra-bot: perf-test: prefetch-broker POC run on staging -> 18% reduction in 95th token latency for chat workload, cost delta +5% steady state (run-id: abc123).

Sourav: rough RPC sketch: ```proto
service PrefetchBroker {
  rpc RequestPrefetch(PrefetchHint) returns (PrefetchLease);
  rpc ReleaseLease(LeaseId) returns (Ack);
}

message PrefetchHint {
  string tenant = 1;
  string hint = 2;
  enum Priority { LOW = 0; NORMAL = 1; HIGH = 2; }
  Priority priority = 3;
  repeated int32 allowed_nodes = 4;
}

message PrefetchLease {
  string lease_id = 1;
  int64 expires_at = 2;
}
```

Katie: also add fields `preferred_node` and `pin_until_seq` (for sequence-based pinning so we can unpin after model step).

Anya: action items: I will draft an RFC with API, quota model, telemetry, and NUMA guidance. volunteers for POC: @Mike, @Sourav. tagging @Thomas for budget policy.

Mike: i'm in :+1:.

Thomas: will take initial budget model.

Anya: thanks — I'll open the PR and a staging perf job by EOD Friday.
